!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-template-parameter-spelled-like-an-absorbed-argument-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10"
  description: """
    Inside an open record a reference's name is read in its `parameters` before the namespace, so a parameter may not
    shadow a schema entry. `base`'s `f: pick<T>` applies `pick` to the entry `T`, and an argument is always a
    reference, so a parameter of `t2` spelled `T` shadows that entry and would change the type of the field `t2`
    absorbs: the shadowing rule refuses it, a resolver error at `t2`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
